      "short": "$P=(\\cos55^{\\circ},-\\sin55^{\\circ})$; $Q=(\\cos80^{\\circ},\\sin80^{\\circ})$; $R=(-\\cos20^{\\circ},-\\sin20^{\\circ})$.",
      "worked": "On the unit circle, the coordinate magnitudes are $\\cos\\theta$ and $\\sin\\theta$, where $\\theta$ is the acute reference angle. Use the quadrant to determine their signs.\n\n$P$ is in Q4, $Q$ is in Q1 and $R$ is in Q3.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=(\\cos55^{\\circ},-\\sin55^{\\circ})\\\\Q&=(\\cos80^{\\circ},\\sin80^{\\circ})\\\\R&=(-\\cos20^{\\circ},-\\sin20^{\\circ}).\\end{align*}$$",
